# The geothermal power plant inside Blush Mountain: turbines turning behind the walls and steam in the pipes. A synth bass
# chugging in sixteenths, a pulse wave running the chords as a sequencer would, a warm pad for the hum of the generators,
# a sawtooth motif calling over it, a four-on-the-floor kit, a wood block ticking and a shaker for the steam.
# One arrangement for day and night, as the plant has no windows.
# Original composition for this game, in the modern sound.
title Power Plant (Alola)
tempo 132
meter 4/4
reverb 0.22
night none
room room 1.0

